    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='Dynamic Array (Generic)',
         body=None,
         narration='Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains the generic dynamic array, in C. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a simple definition. [[slnc 300]] It is an array that grows by itself, written once for any type of element. [[slnc 400]] It is a block of bytes with an element size, and when it is full, it moves into a block twice as big. [[slnc 700]] Our example is a music playlist of songs. [[slnc 400]] By the end, you will know how C builds a growable container for any type, and what it costs.'),
